{"absent":["Monitor side RSI semantics beyond call numbers and status values.","Full runtime patch ordering and SIMD scope acquisition details.","SDEI entry, semihosting console and direct map policy beyond markers."],"dossier":"D11","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi.h::rsi_set_memory_range","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::rsi_set_addr_range_state","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi.h::rsi_set_memory_range_shared","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::rsi_request_version","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::rsi_attestation_token_init","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::rsi_attestation_token_continue"],"text":"Realm range changes apply iteratively until the interval is covered, each step reporting a frontier inside the interval; protected and shared helpers choose RAM versus empty with different destroyed handling, version and config queries use monitor calls, attestation start checks challenge size then returns a handle and continue reports output length for a granule slice."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::RSI_GRANULE_SHIFT","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_cmds.h::ripas","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::RSI_ABI_VERSION_MINOR","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::RSI_SUCCESS","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::SMC_RSI_ABI_VERSION","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::SMC_RSI_IPA_STATE_SET","arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::RSI_ACCEPT"],"text":"RSI uses 4K granules with shift 12; IPA states are empty 0, RAM 1, destroyed 2 and device 3; ABI is major 1 minor 0 with major in the high half; status is success 0, input 1, state 2, incomplete 3 and unknown 4; functions span 0x190 to 0x199; destroyed flags are 0 and 1 with accept 0 and reject 1."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/rsi_smc.h::realm_config","arch/arm64/include/asm/signal32.h::compat_sigcontext","arch/arm64/include/asm/smp.h::ipi_msg_type"],"text":"Realm config is 4K aligned with one union for IPA width and hash choice padded to 512 bytes and another for a 64 byte personalization value padded to 3584 bytes; compat signal state holds trap, mask, ARM registers and fault address with ucontext stack, mask and aligned regspace in frame wrappers; IPI messages list scheduling, calls, stops, timer and work with later special backtrace and debugger types."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/runtime-const.h::runtime_const_ptr","arch/arm64/include/asm/runtime-const.h::__runtime_fixup_mask","arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c::patch_map","arch/arm64/include/asm/rwonce.h::__READ_ONCE"],"text":"Runtime constants record use sites in per symbol sections then patch pointer, shift and mask forms, masks limited to contiguous low ranges; patching maps image text directly and other addresses via page lookup, exit ranges counting as image only before running; single reads use ordered accesses for 1, 2, 4 and 8 bytes with volatile fallback otherwise."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c::__aarch64_insn_write"],"text":"Instruction stores hold a dedicated patch lock with interrupts saved while a fixed slot is installed, written without fault, then released before unlock."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/arm64/kernel/patching.c::aarch64_insn_patch_text_nosync"],"text":"Patch targets must be word aligned or fail as invalid, and success requires cache maintenance over the patched word."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/sdei.h::SDEI_EXIT_HVC","arch/arm64/include/asm/seccomp.h::SECCOMP_ARCH_NATIVE","arch/arm64/include/asm/smp.h::CPU_STUCK_REASON_SHIFT"],"text":"SDEI exit is 0 for HVC and 1 for SMC with IRQ sized stacks; native seccomp is aarch64 with compat arm plus counts, names and 32 bit read, write, exit and sigreturn maps; CPU boot uses MMU off -1 and success 0 with kill, stuck and panic codes and an 8 bit reason field for 52 bit VA and granule failures."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/arm64/include/asm/signal32.h::compat_setup_frame","arch/arm64/include/asm/setup.h::arch_parse_debug_rodata.alt_1","arch/arm64/include/asm/signal.h::arch_untagged_si_addr.alt_1","arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c::set_smp_ipi_range_percpu","arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c::ipi_should_be_nmi","arch/arm64/include/asm/sections.h::entry_tramp_text_size","arch/arm64/kernel/smccc-call.S::arm_smccc_1_2_smc","arch/arm64/include/asm/smp.h::raw_smp_processor_id","arch/arm64/include/asm/smp.h::set_cpu_logical_map"],"text":"Compat frame setup is unsupported and restart does nothing; rodata parsing accepts on, off and noalias and rejects missing or unknown words; fault addresses keep tags for breakpoint traps and are otherwise untagged; IPI setup clamps count, picks shared or per CPU descriptors and arms the boot CPU, using NMI only with priority masking for stop, backtrace and debugger types; trampoline size comes from linker bounds and CPU identity and mapping use current info and stored hardware ids."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/arm-smccc.h::arm_smccc_smc"],"text":"Stub for arm_smccc_smc."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_1"],"text":"Stub for BUG_ON alt 1."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_2"],"text":"Stub for BUG_ON alt 2."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bitops/builtin-__fls.h::__fls"],"text":"Stub for __fls."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_1"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON alt 1."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_2"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON alt 2."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_3"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON alt 3."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON_ONCE alt 1."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON_ONCE alt 2."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3"],"text":"Stub for WARN_ON_ONCE alt 3."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/fixmap.h::clea